      "image": "https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/anthropic_unintended_actions.png",
      "date": "2026-10-18T09:04:39.000Z",
      "summary": "Anthropic's AI model Claude has solved a 25-year-old cryptography puzzle. The mysterious seeds behind NIST's standard curves for digital signatures were provided by the NSA without explanation, raising long-standing suspicion about built-in backdoors. Claude figured out in under 30 minutes that the seeds came from \"lrand48,\" a simple C random number generator, making deliberate backdoors far less likely. The article ",
      "why": "Resolving the origin of the seeds lowers fears that the NSA inserted hidden vulnerabilities into widely used cryptographic standards.",
      "headline": "Claude decodes NSA seed mystery in under 30 minutes",
      "aiSummary": "Anthropic’s model Claude identified the source of mysterious seeds behind NIST’s standard curves for digital signatures in under 30 minutes. Claude found the seeds came from lrand48, a simple C random number generator, reducing suspicion of deliberate backdoors."
