      "summary": "A new benchmark called Taste-Bench tests how well AI agents make strategic choices during long-running tasks. Even the best model, GPT-5.6 Sol, picks the right path on just under 60 percent of simple binary questions. Thinking longer doesn't help. The article AI agents have bad taste in long-term decisions and a new benchmark proves it appeared first on The Decoder .",
      "why": "The benchmark highlights persistent weaknesses in agents’ long-term planning and decision quality.",
      "headline": "New benchmark shows agents struggle with long-term choices",
      "aiSummary": "Taste-Bench tests how well AI agents make strategic choices during long-running tasks. Even the best model, GPT-5.6 Sol, picks the correct path on just under 60 percent of simple binary questions, and thinking longer does not improve performance."
